2. FFmpeg -- REDISTRIBUTED IN THE MOD JAR (LGPL v2.1 or later)
================================================================================
    Project: https://ffmpeg.org/
    Build:   org.bytedeco:ffmpeg:6.0-1.5.9 (JavaCPP Presets, default build)
    License: GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later
    Text:    META-INF/licenses/ffmpeg-COPYING.LGPLv2.1.txt

    The mod jar contains prebuilt FFmpeg shared libraries for windows-x86_64,
    linux-x86_64 and linux-arm64:

        avcodec, avutil, swresample, swscale
        (plus the matching JavaCPP JNI bridge libraries)

    They are used for VP8/VP9 video and Opus audio encoding and decoding.

    IMPORTANT: this is the DEFAULT (non-GPL) JavaCPP Presets FFmpeg build.
    It is configured WITHOUT --enable-gpl, so no GPL-only FFmpeg component
    (such as libx264 or libx265) is present, and the LGPL v2.1+ terms apply.

    The libraries are used as unmodified dynamically loaded shared libraries.
    In accordance with LGPL v2.1 section 6, the corresponding source code and
    the build scripts are available from:

        https://github.com/bytedeco/javacpp-presets/tree/master/ffmpeg
        https://ffmpeg.org/download.html

    Because the libraries are loaded dynamically at runtime, a user may
    replace them with a modified version of FFmpeg by substituting the
    extracted native libraries in the JavaCPP cache directory
    (<gamedir>/wd_javacpp_cache/).

