5. Chromium Embedded Framework / java-cef -- NOT SHIPPED, NOT DOWNLOADED
================================================================================
    Projects: https://bitbucket.org/chromiumembedded/cef
              https://bitbucket.org/chromiumembedded/java-cef
    Licenses: BSD 3-Clause (CEF, java-cef); Chromium is under a mix of BSD
              and other permissive licenses.

    The Chromium/java-cef native binaries are NOT contained in this jar, and
    this mod never fetches them: it contains no networking code of its own.

    On a client, MCEF manages these binaries itself.

    A dedicated server has no MCEF client to do that, so its owner installs
    them by hand into mods/mcef-libraries, once. The exact archive URL, its
    published SHA-256 and the target directory are printed to the server
    console and written into webdisplaystogether-setup.txt. Until they are in
    place the server runs normally and only screens stay disabled.

